{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol | sed -n '1,25p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     2\tpragma solidity 0.8.36;\n     3\t\n     4\timport { IVRFV2PlusWrapper } from \"@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/interfaces/IVRFV2PlusWrapper.sol\";\n     5\timport { IERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\n     6\timport { IERC721 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol\";\n     7\t\n     8\t/// @title raffle.fun Raffle Interface\n     9\t/// @author heesho\n    10\t/// @notice Defines one autonomous NFT raffle using fixed-price USDC entries and one transferable ERC-721 ticket per\n    11\t///         purchase.\n    12\t/// @dev Ticket IDs are sequential. Each ticket stores one inclusive uint128 entry range and remains a transferable\n    13\t///      bearer claim until its owner atomically burns it for redemption or refund. The immutable quote token is trusted\n    14\t///      canonical six-decimal USDC with standard, non-rebasing, fee-free transfers. Supported prizes are honest,\n    15\t///      standards-compliant ERC-721s.\n    16\t/// @custom:version 1.0.0\n    17\tinterface IRaffle {\n    18\t    // Types\n    19\t\n    20\t    /// @notice The single authoritative raffle lifecycle and economic result.\n    21\t    enum Status {\n    22\t        /// @notice The clone is initialized and waiting for the factory to escrow the configured prize.\n    23\t        AwaitingPrize,\n    24\t        /// @notice The prize is escrowed and entry sales or post-sale draw initiation are available.\n    25\t        Active,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"stub\":false,\"stub_explanation\":\"\",\"results\":[{\"flow_summary\":\"A nested invocation is rejected by the shared reentrancy guard before protocol-fee state is read. This is reachable if an external contract called during another nonReentrant raffle operation calls back into releaseProtocolFees; it ends in an atomic ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall revert.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:385 releaseProtocolFees - dispatches the argument-free, permissionless external call through the nonReentrant modifier.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:69 nonReentrant - invokes the guard precheck before entering the function body.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:88 _nonReentrantBeforeView - observes that the shared guard is already ENTERED for a nested invocation.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:90 _nonReentrantBeforeView - reverts with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall before reading or modifying protocolFees.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Reverts with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall; no fee state, token transfer, or release event is reached.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":385,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"There are no calldata arguments. The caller controls the timing and nested execution context that causes the call to encounter an ENTERED guard; no caller-controlled value reaches an asset sink.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This is the reentrancy boundary protecting the permissionless payout from nested execution during external interactions made by other guarded raffle operations.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"A top-level call made while protocolFees is zero fails availability validation. This covers calls before settlement, repeated calls after a completed release, and direct calls to the locked implementation, and ends without transferring funds or emitting a release event.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:385 releaseProtocolFees - dispatches the argument-free call without a caller authorization check and enters the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 _nonReentrantBefore - verifies that the call is not nested and marks the guard ENTERED.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:386 releaseProtocolFees - snapshots the current protocolFees storage value into amount.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:387 releaseProtocolFees - detects amount == 0 and reverts with NoProtocolFees, atomically unwinding the guard update.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Reverts with NoProtocolFees; protocol state and token balances remain unchanged.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":387,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"There are no calldata arguments. The caller controls only when the function observes protocolFees; msg.sender is not used before this revert and no input reaches a transfer sink.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This state-dependent validation prevents empty and duplicate releases and is the only availability check before the payout path.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"With nonzero accrued fees and a valid fixed treasury, the function clears the liability and attempts the external USDC transfer, but a quote-token revert or unsuccessful return terminates the transaction. SafeERC20 propagates or converts the token failure, and EVM rollback restores protocolFees and suppresses the release event.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:385 releaseProtocolFees - accepts any non-reentrant caller; there are no arguments or caller authorization checks.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:386 releaseProtocolFees - snapshots the complete current protocolFees balance.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:387 releaseProtocolFees - passes the nonzero-balance validation.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:388 releaseProtocolFees - sets protocolFees to zero before the external interaction.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:389 releaseProtocolFees - loads the initialization-fixed protocolTreasury; the caller cannot select the recipient.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:390 releaseProtocolFees - dispatches the payout to _transferQuote.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:565 _transferQuote - screens the treasury against known protocol destinations.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:593 _isProtocolDestination - compares fixed protocol addresses, queries the canonical factory implementation getter, and conditionally checks the raffle registry for a code-bearing treasury.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:566 _transferQuote - invokes SafeERC20.safeTransfer on the immutable quote token with treasury and amount.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:184 _safeTransfer - performs the external ERC20 transfer(treasury, amount) call.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:189 _safeTransfer - bubbles a token revert; alternatively SafeERC20.sol:34 rejects a false or otherwise unsuccessful return with SafeERC20FailedOperation.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:388 releaseProtocolFees - the transaction-level revert rolls the earlier zeroing back, leaving the fee claim available for a later attempt.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"The external quote-token transfer fails and the transaction reverts atomically; protocolFees is restored and ProtocolFeesReleased is not emitted.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":566,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller supplies no transfer arguments. Call timing selects the current stored protocolFees snapshot, while both the transfer amount and protocolTreasury recipient are storage-derived; token-side state determines whether the external transfer accepts them.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This is the external asset-transfer failure boundary. Atomic rollback is security-relevant because the contract clears its accounting before calling the trusted token and must preserve the treasury claim if that call fails.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"With nonzero accrued fees, an ordinary non-reentrant call releases the entire balance to the initialization-fixed protocolTreasury. The contract clears protocolFees before interaction, validates the destination, transfers quote tokens, emits ProtocolFeesReleased with the triggering caller, restores the guard, and returns the released amount.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:385 releaseProtocolFees - dispatches the argument-free permissionless entrypoint through nonReentrant.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 _nonReentrantBefore - verifies that the call is not nested and marks the shared guard ENTERED.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:386 releaseProtocolFees - snapshots the complete current protocolFees balance into the return value.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:387 releaseProtocolFees - requires the snapshotted balance to be nonzero.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:388 releaseProtocolFees - clears protocolFees before making an external call.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:389 releaseProtocolFees - loads the initialization-fixed protocolTreasury rather than deriving a recipient from msg.sender.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:390 releaseProtocolFees - dispatches the payout through _transferQuote.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:565 _transferQuote - rejects known protocol destinations before transferring.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:593 _isProtocolDestination - compares the treasury with the raffle, factory, quote token, wrapper, prize token, and implementation, and conditionally queries the factory raffle registry.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:566 _transferQuote - calls SafeERC20.safeTransfer with the fixed treasury and full fee amount.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:176 _safeTransfer - prepares ERC20 transfer(treasury, amount).\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:184 _safeTransfer - performs the external call to the immutable quote-token contract and accepts a true or supported empty successful return.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:391 releaseProtocolFees - emits ProtocolFeesReleased(msg.sender, treasury, amount) after the successful transfer.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:102 _nonReentrantAfter - restores the guard to NOT_ENTERED before amount is returned.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Commits the external ERC20 transfer of the entire accrued fee balance to protocolTreasury, emits ProtocolFeesReleased, and returns amount.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":566,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"There are no calldata arguments. The caller controls transaction timing and msg.sender, which reaches only the indexed caller field of ProtocolFeesReleased. The token-transfer amount comes from protocolFees and the recipient comes from protocolTreasury, so neither is caller-controlled.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This is the sensitive asset-release sink. Review centers on the checks-effects-interactions ordering, fixed-recipient invariant, destination screening, external token call, and accurate event attribution for a permissionless trigger.\"}]}"}}
